Jesus was coming up out of the water. And at that moment, he saw the heavens split open. And he saw the Holy Spirit descend on him like a dove.
A voice came to him from heaven. He said to him, "You are my son, and I love you very much. I am very pleased with you."
Immediately the Spirit drove Jesus into the wilderness.
He was in the desert for 40 days. A temptation from the devil was completed in him. The beasts did not harm Jesus. The angels were guarding him. Jesus chooses the first disciples.
After they seized John, Jesus went to Galilee. He was proclaiming the good news of God.
"The time has come," he said. "The Kingdom of God is near. Repent of your sins and believe in the good news!"
One day Jesus was going to walk by the Sea of Galilee. There he saw Simon and Andrew's brother. They were throwing a net into the lake. They were fishermen.
"Come, follow Me," Jesus said. "I will make you fishers of men."
Immediately they left their nets and followed him.
And Jesus walked a little way. And when he walked, he saw James, the son of Zebedee, and his brother John. They were in a boat mending their nets.
Where did he go? He shouted to them, to them. They left their father Zebdi in the boat with the hired workers. And then they went to follow Jesus. Jesus is driving away someone who is withered.
Jesus and those who were with him went to Capernaum. When the Sabbath came, he entered the synagogue. And he began to teach there.
People were astonished at his teaching. He taught them as one having authority. He did not teach like the teachers of the law.
At that moment, a man in the compound screamed. He was possessed by an evil spirit. He said:
What do you want from us, Jesus of Nazareth? Have you come to destroy us? I know who you are. You are the holy one of God!
"Enough, be quiet!" Jesus said in a firm voice. "Come out of him!"
The evil spirit shook the man violently. Then it came out of him with a scream.
All the people were astonished, and they began to question one another, saying, "What is this? A new teaching! And with authority! Even the demons are subject to him!"
News of Jesus spread quickly throughout Galilee. Jesus saw many people.
Jesus and those who were with him went out from the synagogue. And as they went out, they went with James and John, to the house of Simon and Andrew.
Simon's mom was lying in bed. She had a fever. The doctors told the nurses about this.
Safi went to her. He took her hand and helped her up. The heat subsided for her. And then she started serving them.
In the night following sunset, they brought to Jesus everyone who was sick. They also brought those who were possessed by demons.
All the people in the city gathered at the gate.
Jesus healed many of them. They were sick with all kinds of diseases. He also drove out many demons. But he did not allow the demons to speak, because they knew who he was. Jesus prays in a quiet place.
The dawn was very early and still dark. Jesus got up and went out of the house. He went to a place where he could be alone. There he prayed.
Simon and his companions went to look for Jesus.
When they found him, they cried out, "All the people are fair to you!"
Jesus answered: "Let us go to another town. I want to go to the nearby villages. I must preach there too, as I did when I came."
And Hadi began to travel everywhere in Galilee. He was preaching in their temples. And he was casting out demons. Jesus heals a man who had a skin disease.
A man with a skin disease came to Lesus. He went down on his knees and begged Lesus. He said, "If you want to make me 'clean', you can."
Jesus was filled with profound concern. He reached out and touched the man. "I am willing to do this," he said. "Be clean!"
The disease left him as if he were dead. He recovered.
Jesus took him immediately. He gave him a strong warning.
"Don't tell anyone about this," he said. "He should go show himself to the priest. Make the sacrifices that Moses commanded. He will be a witness before the priest and the people that you are 'clean'."
But the man went out and began to speak immediately. He spread the news to everyone. So Jesus could no longer enter a city publicly. He stayed outside in empty places. But people still came to him from everywhere.
Jesus heals a man who could not walk.
Within a few days after this, Jesus entered again into Capernaum. The people heard that he had come home.
A multitude of people gathered, so that there was no longer any room. There was not even any room outside the door. And Jesus was speaking the word of God to them.
A quarter of those who came were carrying a man who could not walk.
But they couldn't get close to Zeus because of the crowd. So they took an opening on the roof above Zeus. And then they lowered the man through it onto a carpet.
Jesus saw their faith. So he told the man, "Son, your sins are forgiven."
There were some teachers of Sharia who used to sit there. They used to think,
Why is this man talking like this? What does he want to say? Something very bad! Only God can forgive sins!
Immediately Jesus understood what they were thinking in their hearts. And he said to them, "Why are you thinking these things?"
Is it easier for me to say to this man, "Your sins are forgiven"? Or to say, "Stand up, take your mat and walk"?
I want to let you know that he is a good person, he has authority on earth, he forgives sins." And after that, every time Jesus spoke to the man who could not walk.
He told me, "Get up. Take your mat and go home."
The man stood up and took his carpet. When he started to walk, all the people watched him. All the people were amazed. They said, "We have never seen anything like this before!" Jesus Chooses Levi
Again Jesus went out beside the Sea of Galilee. A great crowd came to him. He began to teach them.
As he was walking, he saw Levi, the son of Alphaeus. Levi was sitting in the tax office. Jesus said to him, "Follow me." Levi got up and followed him.
Nafi, after that Jesus was having lunch at the house of Levi. Many tax collectors and "sinners" were eating with him and his disciples. They were among the many people who followed Jesus.
There were some teachers of the law who were Pharisees. They saw Jesus eating with "sinners" and tax collectors. And they asked his disciples: "Why does he eat with tax collectors and 'sinners'?"
Jesus heard that. Therefore, He said to them, "Those who are in good health do not need a physician, but those who are ill do. I did not come to call the righteous, but sinners." Jesus was asked about fasting.
The disciples of John and the Pharisees used to fast. Now the people came to Jesus and said to him, "The disciples of John fast often and make a display of this; and the disciples of the Pharisees also do the same. But your disciples fast neither do they make a display of this. Why do your disciples fast neither do they make a display of this?"
Jesus answered: How can the guests of the bridegroom fast while he is with them? They cannot fast as long as he is with them.
But the time will come when the bridegroom will be taken from them. On that day, they will go without eating.
People shouldn't sew a piece of new cloth onto old clothes. If they do that, the new piece will be tighter than the old one. And it will make the difference bigger.
People don't put new wine into old, rough wineskins, or the wine will burst the skins, and both the wine and the wineskins will be ruined. No, everyone puts new wine into new wineskins." Jesus is the Lord of the Sabbath day.
One Saturday, Jesus was walking with his disciples through the grainfields. His disciples began to pick some heads of grain.
The Pharisees said to Jesus, "Look! It is not lawful to do this on the Sabbath. Why are your disciples doing this?"
Answer, "Have you not read what David did? He and his men were hungry. They needed food."
This was at a time when Abiathar was a high priest. David entered the house of God and ate holy bread. Only priests were allowed to eat it. David gave some of it to his men as well.
Jesus said to them, "The Sabbath was made to serve humanity, not humanity to serve the Sabbath."
So, the Son of Man is also Lord of the Sabbath."
Healing on Saturday.
Again Jesus entered the synagogue. There was a man there whose hand was withered and deformed.
Some Pharisees were trying to find fault with Jesus. They watched him closely. They wanted to see if he would heal the man on the Sabbath day.
Jesus said to the man who had a withered hand and was deformed: "Rise, stand before all the people," he told him.
And Jesus looked at them and asked them: "What does the Law say that we must do on the Sabbath day? Is it lawful to do good? Or to do evil? To save life? Or to kill?" But no one answered Him.
Gan Lizos was looking at them with anger. He was very angry because their hearts were hardened. Then he said to the man: "Stretch out your hand." He stretched it out, and his hand became like the first, sound."
And afterward, the Pharisees went out and began to plot with the Herodians against Jesus, seeking to kill him. The crowds follow Jesus.
Jesus walked with His disciples to the Sea of Galilee. A large crowd from Galilee followed Him.
The people heard about all the things Jesus was doing. Many people came to him. They came from Judea, Jerusalem, and Idumea. They came from the region east of the Jordan River. And they came from the area around Tyre and Sidon.
Because he has little to do with many people, Jesus told his disciples to prepare a small boat for him. This is so that people are not too close to him.
Jesus saw many people. For this reason, those who were sick wanted to come near Him and lay their hands on Him.
When the people possessed by demons saw him, they fell before him. And the demons cried out, "You are the Son of God!"
But Jesus commanded them not to tell who he was. Jesus appoints the twelve apostles.
Jesus came to a certain mountain. He called certain people to come to Him, and they came.
He appointed 12 of them and called them apostles. From then on, they would be with him. And he would send them to preach.
They would have had the power to expel demons.
So Jesus appointed the twelve. Simon was one of them. Jesus gave him the name Peter.
There was James the son of Zebedee and his brother John. Jesus gave them the name Boanerges. Boanerges means Sons of Thunder.
There was also Andrew, and Philip, Bartholomew, Matthew, Thomas, James the son of Alphaeus, and Thaddaeus and Simon the Zealot.
Judas Iscariot was one of them as well. He was the one who would later betray Jesus into the hands of his enemies. Jesus and Beelzebub.
Jesus entered a house. Once again, he gathered the people. The number was so great that Jesus and his disciples could not eat.
His family heard about this. And they went to take him and control him. They said: "This one is not sane."
There were some who studied the law there. They had come from Jerusalem. They said, "This man is driving out demons by the prince of demons! He wants to scatter demons by the power of the chief of demons."
Jesus called out to them and spoke to them in parables. He said, "How can Satan cast out Satan?"
If a kingdom fights itself, it will not last.
If the family is scattered, it cannot endure.
